      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Trunk''' may be:
{{wiktionarypar|trunk}}
*[[Trunk (botany)]], the main structural member of a tree.
*[[Trunk (luggage)]], a large case.
*[[Trunk (automobile)]], a compartment on a car used for storage, called a ''boot'' in British English.
*[[Trunk (motorcycle)]], a case mounted above and behind a motorcycle seat, or the space under the seat
*[[Trunk (telecommunications)]] has a number of closely related meanings.

'''Trunk''' may also refer to:

*[[Torso]], an anatomical term for the human body without the head and limbs.
*The nose of an [[elephant]].

== See also ==

* [[Trunks]] for details of things commonly refered to in the plural.
* [[Trunk shot]] for details of a camera angle.
* [[Trunk road]]

