  <page>
    <title>User information bit</title>
    <id>41842</id>
    <revision>
      <id>25068595</id>
      <timestamp>2005-10-08T17:04:50Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Lerdsuwa</username>
        <id>142668</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>category</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[telecommunication]], an '''user information bit''' is a [[bit]] transferred from a [[source user]] to a telecommunications [[system]] for delivery to a [[destination user]]. 

&lt;i&gt;Note 1:&lt;/i&gt;  [[User information]] bits do not include the overhead bits originated by, or having their primary functional effect within, the telecommunications system. 

&lt;i&gt;Note 2:&lt;/i&gt;  User information bits are encoded to form [[channel bits]].

'''Source:''' From [[Federal Standard 1037C]]

[[Category:Data transmission]]</text>
    </revision>
