  <page>
    <title>Video teleconferencing unit</title>
    <id>41847</id>
    <revision>
      <id>20177608</id>
      <timestamp>2005-08-03T08:55:39Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Martpol</username>
        <id>87217</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>minor edits</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">A '''video teleconferencing unit''' (VTU) is a piece of electrical  equipment that performs [[video teleconference]] functions, such as [[coding]] and decoding of audio and video signals and [[multiplexing]] of video, audio, [[data]], and control signals, and that usually does not include I/O devices, cryptographic devices, [[network interface]] equipment, network connections, or the [[communications network]] to which the unit is connected.

'''Source:''' From [[Federal Standard 1037C]] and from [[MIL-STD-188]]

==External links==
* [http://teleconferencing.ws/ Covering the 3 main conferencing solutions: teleconferencing, video Conferencing and web-based conferencing]



{{com-stub}}</text>
