  <page>
    <title>Terminal</title>
    <id>41892</id>
    <revision>
      <id>40815479</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-23T04:51:14Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>213.226.195.75</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>cswiki</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{Wiktionary}}

The term '''Terminal''' can be used to mean:
* [[Airport terminal]], a building at an airport where passengers transfer from ground transportation to the facilities that allow them to board airplanes

* [[Computer terminal]], an electronic or electromechanical hardware device used for entering data into, and displaying data from, a computer or a computing system.

* [[Container terminal]], a facility which handles shipping.

* [[Dumb terminal]], a computer terminal that has limited functionality relative to other types of &quot;smart&quot; computer terminals.

* [[Pipeline]] terminal, a storage facility at the downstream end of a [[pipeline transport]], typically serving as a buffer between delivery and use

* [[Polymer]] terminal ([[polymer chemistry|chemistry]]), the end [[residue]] on any polymer [[chain]], including [[branch]]es.

* [[RTU|Remote Terminal Unit]], a telemtry device which interfaces objects in the physical world to a [[DCS]] or [[SCADA]] system.

* [[Terminal (electronics)]], a device for joining electrical circuits together.

* [[Terminal illness]], a progressive disease that is expected to cause death.

* [[Terminal object]], a special type of object studied in [[Category Theory]].

* [[Terminal sedation]], the practice of inducing unconsciousness in a terminally ill person for the remainder of the person's life.

* [[Terminal station]], a passenger rail station where rail service begins and ends; the end of the line.

* [[Terminal symbol]], in formal grammar, is a symbol that cannot be further divided.

* [[Terminal (telecommunication)]], a device which is capable of communicating over a line.

* the song &quot;Terminal&quot; by [[Rupert Holmes]], from his first solo album, 1970's ''Widescreen''.

* ''[[The Terminal]]'', a 2004 film by Steven Spielberg, in which a man is stuck in an airport terminal.

'''Terminal''' is a synonym for the following concepts:
* [[Leaf node]], in graphs, trees and computer programs

* [[Computer console]], a text output device for system administration messages

==See also==
* [[Terminus]]

{{disambig}}

