  <page>
    <title>Storage</title>
    <id>41904</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41952870</id>
      <timestamp>2006-03-02T21:19:44Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>GilliamJF</username>
        <id>506179</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* Public storage facilities */ dab key</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Storage''' is the at least semi-permanent holding of an amount of something. A '''storage device''' is an apparatus for holding things. Another general term, is [[container]]. Depending on context it may have a more specific meaning. A [[Tank (disambiguation)|tank]] is a  container for [[liquid]], e.g. [[water]] or [[petroleum]]. In computers it refers to devices that keep data, programs, and other information. 

Storage [[furniture]] includes:
*[[bookcase]]
*[[Cabinet (furniture)|cabinet]]
*[[Chest (furniture)|chest]]
*[[cupboard]]
*[[desk]] (also serves as [[table (furniture)|table]])
*[[sideboard]]/hutch
*[[wardrobe]]

For cool storage a [[Refrigeration|refrigerator]] is used.

For [[archive| archival]] storage, an environment (a room, case, display, etc.) that is [[climate]] controlled (temperature, humidity and light) is required.

A [[closet]] is something between a piece of furniture and a room.

Places in and around the house used for storage, often less suitable as living space, are a [[shed]], a [[cellar]], and an [[attic]]. A [[garage]] is also used as far as not all space is needed for the car, or if it is not used to park a car in. Of these, the cellar tends to be cooler than the rest of the house, which can be an advantage for storage of foods, drinks, batteries, etc.

Storage buildings include a [[warehouse]] and a depot.

One form of [[waste management]] is storing the [[waste]]. See e.g. [[dry cask storage]].

More abstractly:
*In [[physics]], a [[capacitor]] is said to store [[electric charge]].
*[[Book]]s are said to store [[knowledge]], or even [[wisdom]].
*Storage of [[information]] in [[memory]]; also, [[computer]]s, [[hard drive]]s and [[random access memory|RAM]] are said to store information, (see [[Computer storage]]).

See also [[hoarding]].

==Public storage facilities==
A facility to store clothing, bags, suitcases, or various belongings is often provided in [[train station]]s, [[Theater (structure)|theatre]]s, [[school]]s, [[swimming pool]]s, [[sauna]]s, [[library|libraries]], etc., and sometimes in [[shop]]s.

It may be called left-luggage, cloakroom, locker room, etc.

For [[access control]] there may either be an attendant who provides a [[ticket]], or a storage compartment can be locked with a [[key (lock)|key]] (a traditional key or a keycard), or it has a combination lock. Sometimes a [[fingerprint]] [[scanner]] is used.

The facility is sometimes compulsory for large bags and for coats in a museum or shop, to prevent theft.

The facility may be free of charge or require a fee; even if it is free of charge, one may have to pay a [[deposit]] for the key.

In swimming pools and saunas the key is attached to a [[strap]], to be attached to a [[wrist]] or [[ankle]].

See also [[changeroom]].

[[Self-storage]] is storage space rentable for a fee.

[[de:Speicher]]
[[es:Memoria]]
[[ia:Memoria]]</text>
    </revision>
