    <title>Franz Mertens</title>
    <id>41999</id>
    <revision>
      <id>28943147</id>
      <timestamp>2005-11-22T00:01:36Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Michael Hardy</username>
        <id>4626</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Franz Mertens''' ([[March 20]], [[1840]] - [[March 5]], [[1927]]) was a [[Germany|German]] [[mathematician]]. He was born in [[Środa Wielkopolska|Środa]] in the [[Grand Duchy of Poznań]], [[Kingdom of Prussia]] (now Środa Wielkopolska, [[Poland]]) and died in [[Vienna]], [[Austria]].

The [[Mertens function]] is the sum function for the [[Möbius function]], in the theory of [[arithmetic function]]s. The [[Mertens conjecture]] concerning its growth, conjecturing it bounded by ''x''&lt;sup&gt;1/2&lt;/sup&gt;, which would have implied the [[Riemann hypothesis]], is now known to be false ([[Andrew Odlyzko|Odlyzko]] and te Riele, 1985).  The [[Meissel-Mertens constant]] is analogous to the [[Euler-Mascheroni constant]], but the [[harmonic series (mathematics)|harmonic series]] sum in its definition is only over the [[prime number|primes]] rather than over all integers.

See also: [[Mertens' theorems]].

==External links==
* {{MacTutor Biography|id=Mertens}}

