      <text xml:space="preserve">'''''Ad Gentes''''' is the [[Second Vatican Council|Second Vatican Council's]] '''Decree on the Missionary Activity of the Church'''.  Passed by the assembled bishops by a vote of 2,394 to 5, it was promulgated by [[Pope Paul VI]] on [[November 18]], [[1965]].  The title is [[Latin]] for &quot;To the Nations,&quot; and is from the first line of the decree, as is customary with [[Catholic Church|Roman